# Brewfile.local — packages THIS Mac keeps that the repo does not declare.
#
# Copied to ~/.config/chez/Brewfile.local on your first apply. It lives
# outside the checkout on purpose: it is your machine's answer, not the
# repo's, so it is never committed and never shows up in `git status`.
#
# It is read as one more Brewfile tier, which means a package listed here is
# declared in exactly the sense a repo package is:
#
#   chez doctor   stops reporting it as untracked
#   chez mirror   never offers it for uninstall
#   chez up       installs it if it is missing
#
# Deleting a line hands the package straight back — it becomes untracked again
# on the next run, and the removal verbs will offer it. That round trip is the
# point: diverging from the repo is allowed, as long as it is written down.
#
# Add entries with `chez adopt --local <package>`, or by hand in the same syntax
# as any Brewfile:
#
#   brew "ffmpeg"
#   cask "obs"
#   tap  "some/tap"
#
# If you find yourself copying the same line into this file on every Mac, it
# belongs in features/brew/Brewfile instead — `chez adopt <package>`.

